<title>FRANCE: EU sells about 25,000 T each of German barley, rye.</title>
<headline>EU sells about 25,000 T each of German barley, rye.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday sold 24,776 tonnes of German intervention barley at a minimum price of 104.53 Ecus per tonne for export to countries outside the EU, grain operators said.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committee in Brussels also sold 25,392 tonnes of German intervention rye at a minimum price of 100.52 Ecus per tonne, they said.</p>
</text>
